  "query_preview": "/Friday through Monday/... \nMuch quieter weather is expected starting Friday with much drier \nair in place behind the departing trough. Another follow-on \nshortwave is likely to dive in from the northwest late Friday into\nSaturday with guidance indicating that this shortwave will become\na cutoff low over AZ as it detaches from the main jet stream \nenergy. At this time, this feature is likely to be inconsequential\ngiven that there will be an abundance of dry air in place \nlimiting any additional rainfall potential. Under the general \ntroughing influence, afternoon high temperatures through the \nupcoming weekend will remain below normal. Coolest day is expected\non Friday when much of the lower deserts struggle to reach 80 \ndegrees for afternoon highs.",
